

*EXP. No. 3(a) & 3(b)*

*AIM:* (a) To check if argument is file/directory and positive/negative/zero (b) To convert file names to uppercase.



*• #!/bin/bash -*
First line, called shebang. Tells system to use bash shell to run script.

*• chmod +x file.sh -*
Adds execute permission to run script. Without it ./file.sh will not work.

*• $0, $1, $# -*
`$0` - script name
`$1` - first argument capture, captures what you type after script name
`$#` - total number of arguments capture

*• $@ -*
Captures all command line arguments passed to script as group but treats them separately. Used in for loop to take all files.

*• ./file.sh / bash file.sh -*
To run the script. ./ needs execute permission, bash file.sh works without permission.

*• if, elif, else, fi -*
`if` checks condition, `elif` checks second condition, `else` if all false, `fi` is end of block.

*• -f, -d -*
File test operators used inside if [ ]
`-f` checks if the given path is file
`-d` check if the given path is directory

*• -eq, -ne, -lt, -le, -gt, -ge -*
Integer comparison operators used inside [ ]
`-eq` : equal
`-ne` : not equal
`-lt` : less than / smaller than
`-le` : less than or equal
`-gt` : greater than
`-ge` : greater than or equal

*• tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]' -*
Translate or convert small letter to Capital [a-z] to [A-Z].
`tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'` - Converts Capital [A-Z] to small [a-z].

*• for loop -*
It is used to repeat the task for each file. `for name in "$@"`

*• mv -*
It means move or rename the file. Used to save after converting.

*• | - Pipe -*
It take output of first command and give it as input for second one.

*• > - Redirection -*
Sends output into a file. Used to store converted content.
